::SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.DIG.01
Question:
A class needs to share quick instructions for joining an online speech rehearsal. Which digital format best fits the audience need?
{
~A. A long essay explaining the history of online meetings.#This format does not match the audience need. Students need quick instructions, not background information.
=B. A short digital checklist with the meeting link and steps.#Correct. A checklist fits the purpose because it gives students clear, usable steps for joining the rehearsal.
~C. A decorative poster with no link or instructions.#This may look interesting, but it fails the communication purpose. The audience needs practical joining information.
~D. A transcript of a full speech about technology.#This gives too much unrelated information. Audience-aware digital publication should select the format that helps users act.
}
::SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.03
Question:
Which choice best shows audience awareness for parents receiving an email about a presentation night?
{
~A. Use slang and inside jokes from class.#This tone may confuse or exclude parents. Audience awareness means choosing language that fits the readers and setting.
~B. Put the location at the very bottom after several unrelated details.#This hides important information. Parents need key event details placed where they can find them easily.
~C. Use vague wording such as "come to the thing later."#This does not communicate clearly. Audience-aware communication should make the event, time, and purpose specific.
=D. Use a clear subject line, respectful tone, date, location, and contact information.#Correct. This choice fits the audience because it gives parents the information they need in a professional, usable form.
}
::SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q03::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.PRES.02
Question:
Why should a slide deck about interview preparation use brief headings and simple visuals?
{
=A. They help the audience follow key points while the speaker explains details aloud.#Correct. The visuals support the presentation by guiding attention without replacing the speaker's explanation.
~B. They make it possible for the speaker to avoid explaining anything.#This misunderstands presentation support. Visuals should work with the speaker, not replace communication.
~C. They guarantee that every audience member will agree with the message.#This overclaims. Good visuals improve clarity, but they cannot guarantee agreement.
~D. They allow the presenter to include every detail on one slide.#This creates overload. Strong digital presentation design organizes information so the audience can follow it.
}
::SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q04::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.DIG.01
Question:
Which design choice best supports accessibility in a digital publication?
{
~A. Use tiny text so more information fits on the page.#Tiny text makes the message harder to read. Accessibility requires the audience to see and use the information clearly.
~B. Use low contrast colors because they look subtle.#Low contrast can make text difficult to read. A clear publication uses readable contrast for the audience.
=C. Use readable text size, clear headings, and strong contrast.#Correct. These choices help the audience read, scan, and understand the digital publication more easily.
~D. Remove headings so the page looks less structured.#Headings support scanning and organization. Removing them can make the message harder for the audience to use.
}
::SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q05::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L06_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.03
Question:
Which question should a communicator ask before selecting a digital format?
{
~A. Which format lets me add the most decoration?#Decoration is not the first concern. The format should be chosen because it helps the audience understand and use the message.
=B. Who is the audience, and what do they need to know first?#Correct. Audience and priority information should guide the digital format, organization, and design choices.
~C. How can I make the message longer?#Length does not guarantee clarity. Audience-aware communication uses enough information, organized for the user's needs.
~D. Which platform is newest or most popular?#Popularity alone is not enough. The best platform is the one that fits the audience, purpose, and communication context.
}
